# Open Library (books) — REST, no key and no OAuth.
#
# There is no API key at all. Open Library instead asks every client to send a
# User-Agent that identifies the app and a contact address; anonymous clients
# get rate-limited hard. The app sends the same string from OpenLibraryProvider.

@userAgent = MediaArchive (https://github.com/bragehs/MediaArchive; brage.skjorestad@gmail.com)
@fields = key,title,author_name,first_publish_year,cover_i,number_of_pages_median,ratings_average,ratings_count,subject

### Search works by free text
GET {{openLibraryBaseUrl}}/search.json?q=final+empire&fields={{fields}}&limit=5
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Search by title + author (field-scoped query)
GET {{openLibraryBaseUrl}}/search.json?q=title:mistborn+author:sanderson&fields={{fields}}&limit=5
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### Look up by ISBN
GET {{openLibraryBaseUrl}}/search.json?q=isbn:9780441172719&fields={{fields}}&limit=5
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### The same row the provider reads back in GetByIdAsync — search index by work key
GET {{openLibraryBaseUrl}}/search.json?q=key:/works/OL893415W&fields={{fields}}&limit=1
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}

### The work record — this is the only endpoint carrying the description
GET {{openLibraryBaseUrl}}/works/OL893415W.json
User-Agent: {{userAgent}}
